<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n49071" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">trĭĕtēris</span></b> ,
			ĭdis, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τριετηρίς.</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i>a space of three
			years</i>, <i>three years</i>, <i><span class="en">Stat. S. 2,
				6, 72</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mart. 9, 85, 9</span></i>; <i><span class="en">10, 53, 3</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Aus. Caes. 3</span></i>. —
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>a triennial
				festival;</i> of the festival of Bacchus, <i><span class="en">Cic. N. D.
				3, 23, 58</span></i>; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">trietericus.—Of the Nemean games,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Th. 4, 722</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">7, 93</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
